launching user's other access.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time\",\n          \"owner\": \"R11\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\",\n          \"owner\": \"E12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\",\n          \"owner\": \"A02\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/agent/identity.ts\",\n          \"line\": 49,\n          \"note\": \"Both IDs are required on every audit record (recorder.ts:12-13) and the type ID matches release/manifest.json:3. But the instance ID is a random UUID per process with no pod name, node or registry behind it. Only a startup log at server.ts:37 pairs it with the release, and the reminders job (workers/reminders.ts) logs nothing. An operator cannot go from an instance ID to a live pod from this repo.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Each audit record carries the agent-type-id and agent-instance-id, which resolve to a stored deployment manifest and a live instance.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check `agent.type.id` and `agent.instance.id` are written on every record. 3) Check the type ID can be looked up to a stored manifest (registry, manifest store, file keyed by hash). 4) Answer no if either field is missing or nothing stores manifests by that ID. Answer unknown if the lookup store is outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/identity.ts:49\",\n          \"quote\": \"export const AGENT_INSTANCE_ID = randomUUID();\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Both IDs are required on every audit record (recorder.ts:12-13) and the type ID matches release/manifest.json:3. But the instance ID is a random UUID per process with no pod name, node or registry behind it. Only a startup log at server.ts:37 pairs it with the release, and the reminders job (workers/reminders.ts) logs nothing. An operator cannot go from an instance ID to a live pod from this repo.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.2\",\n          \"check\": \"An ownership record in code or config maps each agent type to a responsible team and a current operator or on-call rotation.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Look for CODEOWNERS, `catalog-info.yaml`, `.brace/deployment.yaml`, or another ownership file. 2) Check each agent type maps to a team and to a current operator or on-call rotation. 3) Answer no if an agent type has no owner, or owners exist only in prose with no link. Answer unknown if ownership lives in an outside catalog.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/config.ts:64\",\n          \"quote\": \"operationalOwner: \\\"team:agent-platform\\\",\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Owner and operator are constants written to every audit record (config.ts:63-64) and CODEOWNERS names teams. The on-call rotation appears only in README prose (#agent-platform-oncall) and an SSO group pattern in iam.tf:69. The roster itself is outside this repo, and ownership is not keyed by agent type.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.3\",\n          \"check\": \"A containment control can disable a single instance or a single agent type (for example revoke its principal or scale it to zero) without touching the launching user's credentials.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find stop and revoke controls: admin endpoints, CLIs, feature flags, scale-to-zero, per-instance token revocation. 2) Check their scope is one instance or one agent type. 3) Answer no if the only control is a global switch or revoking a shared or user credential. Answer unknown if containment is run by an outside platform.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/control/kill-switch.ts:57\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (halted.has(\\\"global\\\")) throw new Halted(\\\"global\\\");\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Stop flags exist only for pk global or tenant#<clinicId> (kill-switch.ts:28, 57-58). No control targets one instance or one agent type. The server and reminders job share one type ID, one IAM role (iam.tf:14-17) and one namespace. A halt hits the whole fleet or a whole clinic. Also, the runtime role can PutItem on clinic-agent-control (iam.tf:47), so a compromised instance could clear its own halt.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"contain the right instance or agent type\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Stop controls reach only the whole fleet or one clinic, and an instance ID cannot be traced to a live pod.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Add per-instance and per-agent-type halt keys to the control table and checks, record the pod name with the instance ID, and keep a lookup from type ID to stored manifest and owner.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"operations\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A06\",\n      \"gate\": \"G3\",\n      \"title\": \"Parent and prompt provenance\",\n      \"requirement\": \"For every sub-agent, record its own type and instance IDs, a link to its parent, trace links, and the prompt the parent gave it. Trace a nested action back to that prompt. Protect sensitive prompt text with restricted storage and a clear redaction policy. Standard GenAI instrumentation records prompts only when you turn that on, so confirm it is on for this path.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Sub-agent given powers beyond its task\",\n          \"owner\": \"E08\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Children still running after the parent is stopped\",\n          \"owner\": \"E09\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No limit on how many sub-agents a run can start\",\n          \"owner\": \"B07\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts\",\n          \"line\": 35,\n          \"note\": \"The eligibility peer is a delegated agent task over A2A (eligibility-a2a.ts:65 message/send). The harness assigns the peer no type or instance ID. The record holds only the static string eligibility-agent.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A06.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Each sub-agent gets its own type ID and instance ID, assigned by the harness when it is started.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find sub-agent spawn code (handoffs, subgraphs, subagents, A2A task creation). 2) Check the harness assigns the child a new `agent.instance.id` and a type ID at start. 3) Answer no if any spawn path reuses the parent's IDs, assigns none, or takes the IDs from the model's request.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:35\",\n          \"quote\": \"detail: { peer: \\\"eligibility-agent\\\", status: result.status, depositWaived: result.depositWaived },\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The eligibility peer is a delegated agent task over A2A (eligibility-a2a.ts:65 message/send). The harness assigns the peer no type or instance ID. The record holds only the static string eligibility-agent.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A06.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Each sub-agent's records include its direct parent's instance ID and a trace link to the parent.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open sub-agent spawn code and the child's record writer. 2) Look for a parent instance field (for example `agent.parent.instance_id`) and trace propagation (span parent, span link, `traceparent` in queued payloads). 3) Answer no if any spawn path, including remote or queued, starts a fresh trace or omits the parent ID.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:61\",\n          \"quote\": \"headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \\\"content-type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", traceparent: opts.traceparent },\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"traceparent is propagated, but the request sends no parent agent.instance.id. The audit record for the call has no child trace or span link.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A06.3\",\n          \"check\": \"The prompt the parent passed to the child is captured on this path, with prompt capture switched on in config rather than left at the default off.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where the parent's prompt to the child is recorded (for example `agent.parent.prompt`, or a hash plus stored text). 2) Check prompt content capture is turned on in config, for example a GenAI capture-content env var or SDK option. 3) Answer no if capture is left at its default off, or the setting falls back to false when unset.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:35\",\n          \"quote\": \"detail: { peer: \\\"eligibility-agent\\\", status: result.status, depositWaived: result.depositWaived },\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The message sent to the peer (eligibility-a2a.ts:62-72) is never recorded. No capture-content setting exists anywhere in src, config, k8s or the workflows.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A06.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Captured prompt text is stored with restricted access and a redaction policy, and only an approved audit role can read it.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where captured prompt text is stored (bucket, table, log index). 2) Check its IAM or ACL limits reads to an approved audit role. 3) Check a redaction policy is defined and applied. 4) Answer no if prompts go to general logs the whole team can read, or no redaction exists. Answer unknown if storage access is set outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts:50\",\n          \"quote\": \"detail: z.record(z.unknown()).optional(),\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No parent prompt is captured, so there is no prompt store to check. Audit goes to an object-lock bucket (main.tf:134) with no bucket policy in this repo, and there is no redaction policy for peer prompts.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"record its own type and instance IDs, a link to its parent, trace links, and the prompt the parent gave it\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"The A2A eligibility peer is a delegated agent task with no child IDs, no parent instance link and no captured prompt.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Assign and record child type and instance IDs for the peer call, send the parent instance ID with the trace link, and capture the delegated message with restricted storage and redaction.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A07\",\n      \"gate\": \"G3\",\n      \"title\": \"Every model in the loop\",\n      \"requirement\": \"List all helper models, such as verifiers, judges, rerankers, and world models. Give each one an identity based on its available model version or digest, its prompt, and its configuration, and record which decisions it made. Show that a swapped, drifting, or failing checker counts as a failure of the control that depends on it.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Main agent model changing behind a fixed name unnoticed\",\n          \"owner\": \"C05\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Second-model review not tested against evasive behavior\",\n          \"owner\": \"R10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Self-hosted model weights loaded without a signature or format check\",\n          \"owner\": \"C05\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"likely_pass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"release/manifest.json\",\n          \"line\": 29,\n          \"note\": \"The only helper model is the intent classifier. It has its own record in the manifest inventory, matching src/config.ts:50.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A07.1\",\n          \"check\": \"A model inventory in code or config lists every helper model the agent calls (verifiers, judges, rerankers, embedding models, world models).\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search for every model call: provider SDK clients, model name strings, embedding, rerank, moderation, and judge calls. 2) Compare that list with the model inventory. 3) Answer no if any helper model called in code is missing from the inventory, or no inventory exists.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"release/manifest.json:29\",\n          \"quote\": \"\\\"requestedId\\\": \\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\",\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src, package.json, k8s and workflows for model, embed, rerank, moderat, judge, anthropic, openai. Only classifier.ts:45 and loop.ts:61 call a model; countTokens (context-size.ts:35) is not a separate model. No embedding or rerank dependency in package.json.\",\n          \"note\": \"The only helper model is the intent classifier. It has its own record in the manifest inventory, matching src/config.ts:50.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"I11c134ddd9 classifier model call\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/classifier.ts:45\",\n              \"quote\": \"res = await client.messages.create(\",\n              \"note\": \"Helper model (intent classifier). Has a record in the manifest model inventory (release/manifest.json role intent_classifier) and a constant in src/config.ts:50.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"Iacad2084b6 main agent model call\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:61\",\n              \"quote\": \"const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\",\n              \"note\": \"Main agent model, not a helper. Listed in the manifest as role agent.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"classifier inventory record\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"release/manifest.json:29\",\n              \"quote\": \"\\\"requestedId\\\": \\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\",\",\n              \"note\": \"Inventory record for the only helper model; matches CLASSIFIER_MODEL in src/config.ts:50.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"context-size.ts countTokens call\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/context-size.ts:35\",\n              \"quote\": \"const r = await client.messages.countTokens(req, { signal });\",\n              \"note\": \"Token count of the main agent's own request. It makes no decision and loads no separate model.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"eligibility peer agent (A2A)\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:6\",\n              \"quote\": \"// Insurance-eligibility peer agent, reached over A2A (JSON-RPC message/send).\",\n              \"note\": \"Remote agent run by another team. This repo makes no model call for it. Its delegation is reviewed under A06.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"reminders worker\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/workers/reminders.ts:7\",\n              \"quote\": \"import { render, sms } from \\\"../integrations/sms.js\\\";\",\n              \"note\": \"Imports no model SDK; sends templated SMS only.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A07.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Each helper model is identified by a pinned version or digest plus its prompt and configuration, not by an alias.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) For each helper model, find its model ID and follow env vars to the final value. 2) Check it is a pinned version or digest, and that its prompt and configuration are also recorded. 3) Answer no if any is an alias (`-latest`, undated name), falls back to one by default, or is hard-coded inline outside the inventory.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/config.ts:50\",\n          \"quote\": \"export const CLASSIFIER_MODEL = \\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\";\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for env overrides, -latest or undated names and a second hard-coded classifier ID. Found none; the ID comes only from this constant.\",\n          \"note\": \"Dated snapshot. Prompt digest is in the manifest and CI-checked. Request config and a CLASSIFIER_ID hash over model, prompt and config are in classifier.ts:14-22. The 0.6 threshold (classifier.ts:39) is control policy and is not in the hash.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"classifier model ID\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/config.ts:50\",\n              \"quote\": \"export const CLASSIFIER_MODEL = \\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\";\",\n              \"note\": \"Dated snapshot constant. No env override and no alias fallback; the only use is classifier.ts:47 and identity.ts:30.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"classifier model ID in manifest\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"release/manifest.json:31\",\n              \"quote\": \"\\\"versionDoc\\\": { \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\\\", \\\"checked\\\": \\\"2026-09-15\\\" },\",\n              \"note\": \"Manifest labels it a pinned snapshot with provider doc and date.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"classifier prompt\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"release/manifest.json:14\",\n              \"quote\": \"{ \\\"path\\\": \\\"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\\\"\",\n              \"note\": \"Prompt digest recorded in the manifest and compared to the file by ci.yml manifest-check.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"classifier configuration\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/classifier.ts:14\",\n              \"quote\": \"export const CLASSIFIER_CONFIG = { max_tokens: 64, temperature: 0, timeoutMs: 4000 } as const;\",\n              \"note\": \"Request configuration is in version control and hashed into CLASSIFIER_ID.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"classifier identity hash\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/classifier.ts:16\",\n              \"quote\": \"export 