\"subject\": \"production deploy job\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:37\",\n              \"quote\": \"environment: ${{ inputs.emergency && 'production-emergency' || 'production' }}\",\n              \"note\": \"The only deploy job always runs in a protected environment.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"production environment reviewers\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf:44\",\n              \"quote\": \"prevent_self_review = true\",\n              \"note\": \"Reviewers are the agent-platform-leads team (line 42); branches limited to protected ones (line 46).\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"emergency environment reviewers\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf:67\",\n              \"quote\": \"branch_pattern = \\\"hotfix/*\\\"\",\n              \"note\": \"Emergency environment also requires leads (line 55) with prevent_self_review (line 57).\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"deploy role trust\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf:82\",\n              \"quote\": \"\\\"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production\\\",\",\n              \"note\": \"Role assumable only from the two environments (line 83 is the emergency one).\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"cluster write access\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/main.tf:50\",\n              \"quote\": \"principal_arn = aws_iam_role.deploy.arn\",\n              \"note\": \"Only the deploy role has edit access to the clinic-agent namespace.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"config path ownership\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \".github/CODEOWNERS:5\",\n              \"quote\": \"/config/             @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\",\n              \"note\": \"/release/, /prompts/, /k8s/, /infra/ and /.github/ are also named roles (lines 4,6-9). The catch-all * (line 3) owns code only.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"agent runtime credentials\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf:41\",\n              \"quote\": \"\\\"dynamodb:GetItem\\\",\",\n              \"note\": \"Runtime role has no ECR, EKS, S3 or IAM write, so it cannot change manifest, prompts, k8s or policy files. It can write the clinic-agent-* state tables (iam.tf:47), which is raised outside this check.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": [\n            {\n              \"category\": \"unprotected branch deploy\",\n              \"input\": \"Dispatch deploy.yml from a feature branch with emergency=false\",\n              \"trace\": \"The job uses environment production, whose branch policy allows protected branches only; a feature branch is not protected so the run is refused before secrets or the role are available.\",\n              \"outcome\": \"blocked\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf:46\",\n              \"quote\": \"protected_branches     = true\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"category\": \"emergency without approval\",\n              \"input\": \"Developer pushes hotfix/x and dispatches with emergency=true\",\n              \"trace\": \"Environment production-emergency allows hotfix/* but requires a reviewer from agent-platform-leads and forbids self review, so the job waits and cannot assume the role until a lead approves.\",\n              \"outcome\": \"blocked\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf:57\",\n              \"quote\": \"prevent_self_review = true\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"category\": \"other workflow assumes role\",\n              \"input\": \"A different workflow tries to assume clinic-agent-deploy through OIDC\",\n              \"trace\": \"The trust policy requires the sub claim to equal one of two environment values, which only jobs running in those environments present.\",\n              \"outcome\": \"blocked\",\n              \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/github.tf:83\",\n              \"quote\": \"\\\"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production-emergency\\\",\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"C02.3\",\n          \"check\": \"An emergency change path exists that records an owner, a reason, an end date, and a follow-up review.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search for an emergency or break-glass path (runbook, workflow, CLI). 2) Check it records owner, reason, end date, and follow-up review. 3) Answer no if any of the four is missing, or the path bypasses review with no record. Answer unknown if the procedure lives outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:83\",\n          \"quote\": \"if: inputs.emergency\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The emergency path records owner, reason and end date as inputs and opens a follow-up issue. But the issue step has no always() condition and runs after kubectl apply and rollout status (deploy.yml:71-80). If the rollout wait fails, the change is live and no follow-up review is opened. The end date check (deploy.yml:50) accepts any string date -d parses, including past dates.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Record emergency changes with an owner, a reason, an end date, and a follow-up review\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Reviews and environments are well gated, but the emergency follow-up issue is skipped when the rollout step fails.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Run the follow-up step with if: always() on emergency runs, validate expires_on as a future date, and check the owner is a real account.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"governance\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"injection_attempts\": [],\n  \"prescan_resolutions\": {\n    \"H005\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": \"C02\",\n      \"reason\": \"Wildcard is on ecr:GetAuthorizationToken in the deploy role (github.tf:98-100), which AWS only allows on *. The role is not the agent's runtime identity and is assumable only from the protected environments.\"\n    },\n    \"H006\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": \"A07\",\n      \"reason\": \"loop.ts:36 writes run.started before the try. The classifier audit at loop.ts:42 runs after every classifier outcome, and the catch at loop.ts:106-110 audits the stop. Not a success-only audit for this batch.\"\n    },\n    \"H007\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": \"A07\",\n      \"reason\": \"loop.ts:36 writes run.started before the try. The classifier audit at loop.ts:42 runs after every classifier outcome, and the catch at loop.ts:106-110 audits the stop. Not a success-only audit for this batch.\"\n    },\n    \"H008\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": \"A05\",\n      \"reason\": \"loop.ts:106 try wraps the run.stopped audit in the error handler. An audit failure there is logged and the run still hands off. Every record carries the identity fields via ident().\"\n    },\n    \"H009\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": \"A05\",\n      \"reason\": \"executor.ts:51 and :93 audit denied and failed calls too, and AuditUnavailable is rethrown at executor.ts:92. Identity fields come from base (executor.ts:42). Audit-completeness is R13's item.\"\n    },\n    \"H010\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": \"A05\",\n      \"reason\": \"executor.ts:51 and :93 audit denied and failed calls too, and AuditUnavailable is rethrown at executor.ts:92. Identity fields come from base (executor.ts:42). Audit-completeness is R13's item.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"repo\": \"\",","   \"commit\": null,","   \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-20T15:36:27Z\",","-  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",","+  \"scope\": \"Batch review of A05, A06, A07, C01 and C02 only, by claude-sonnet-5-5, normal mode (no --conservative). Reviewed the whole clinic-agent repo as data: src, config, release/manifest.json, k8s, Dockerfile, infra/terraform, .github (CODEOWNERS, ci.yml, deploy.yml), prompts and README. No .brace/ folder exists. Not run: the agent, tests, terraform, or any network call; GitHub and AWS settings were read from terraform, not confirmed live. Prescan hits H005-H010 were resolved because they touch these items; H001-H004 (B11) and H011 (E03) belong to other batches and are left open. The fresh challenge/hunt step was not run, so the one likely_pass (A07) is unchallenged and the other 47 items are unreviewed.\",","   \"review_protocol\": \"coverage-first-v1\",","   \"findings\": [","     {"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S3LaQtyChGKRtPExweUh1i","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
