{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDkBhnraMGMAM6br5sNw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed A05, A06, A07, C01 and C02. The findings file is saved at `agent/brace-findings.json` and passes `--batch A05,A06,A07,C01,C02 --before-challenges --fix` (\"Valid. gap: 4, likely_pass: 1\"). I ran no challenges and did not run the repo.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 | gap | Stop flags exist only for `global` or one clinic (`src/control/kill-switch.ts:57`), so nothing contains one instance or one agent type. The instance ID is a random per-process UUID (`src/agent/identity.ts:49`) with no pod link. |\n| A06 | gap | The A2A eligibility peer is a delegated agent task. The harness assigns it no IDs, sends no parent instance ID (only `traceparent`), and never captures the message it sends (`src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:35`). |\n| A07 | likely_pass | The only helper model is the Haiku classifier. It is a dated snapshot with its prompt and config hashed into an ID. Every outcome is audited with its identity (`src/agent/loop.ts:42`), and every failure path routes to staff. |\n| C01 | gap | The manifest has no identity bindings (issuers and audiences). Most artifacts have no owner, and the config, policy and budget files are referenced by path with no digest. |\n| C02 | gap | Branch protection and the protected environments are solid. But the emergency follow-up issue step has no `always()` (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml:83`), so it is skipped if the rollout wait fails after `kubectl apply`. The `expires_on` check also accepts past dates. |\n\n- **Unknown checks:** A05.2 (the on-call roster is outside the repo) and A06.4 (no captured prompt text exists to check).\n- **Prescan hits:** I resolved H005–H010 as dismissed, with reasons. I left H001–H004 (B11) and H011 (E03) open for their own batches.\n- **Not in this batch:** The runtime IAM role can `PutItem` on the `clinic-agent-*` tables, including the control (kill-switch) and approvals tables (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:47`). `src/agent/classifier.ts:51` doesn't escape patient text, unlike the main loop. `eligibility-check.ts:40` auto-refunds a deposit without the staff approval that `config/policy.yaml` requires for `payments__refund_deposit`. Whoever reviews B02, R10, R11 and the approval items should look at these.\n- **Judgment calls:** C02.3 as `no` is a judgment call (medium confidence). I kept C02.2 as `yes` because the IAM write is to state tables, not config, but `src/config.ts` and `src/agent` are owned only by the developer group.\n- **Remaining step:** The A07 likely_pass is unchallenged. The scope field says so.\n\nMy ledger input files are in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":137206,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439},"output_tokens":789,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45ab43c4-ecdd-452d-b4e1-a84e9bc45d3f","uuid":"05978ed1-4981-48b4-9885-9372e1b79de2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:43:26.495Z","request_id":"req_011CgDkBhWEd1wC7KqMiG27k"}
